1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:07,259
There are two ways to add students: one at a time, or many at once from a spreadsheet. We show both.

2
00:00:08,686 --> 00:00:11,694
Open Students in the menu and click Add student.

3
00:00:13,258 --> 00:00:23,124
Enter the enrollment number and the full name. The enrollment number must be unique, because the student will use it to sign in. Here we add Aarav Sharma.

4
00:00:25,855 --> 00:00:30,090
In the Cohort field, choose his section: Class 10, Section A.

5
00:00:31,432 --> 00:00:35,189
Click Add student. Aarav's page opens, with his section.

6
00:00:37,479 --> 00:00:46,144
To let Aarav create his own password, click Issue activation code. The code is shown only once: give it to the student or print it.

7
00:00:48,706 --> 00:00:55,959
Now the faster way. Open Imports. You can upload a CSV or Excel file with one row for each student.

8
00:00:58,161 --> 00:01:06,717
We upload a file with some mistakes on purpose: a missing name, an enrollment number written twice, and a section that doesn't exist.

9
00:01:10,317 --> 00:01:16,616
ScoreCode checks every row first and saves nothing yet. Each problem is listed with its row and a reason.

10
00:01:19,438 --> 00:01:27,184
Correct the file and click Upload fixed file. You can also download the checked file to see the problems inside your spreadsheet.

11
00:01:29,007 --> 00:01:34,704
Now every row is correct. ScoreCode tells you exactly how many new students will be added.

12
00:01:35,510 --> 00:01:39,516
Only now does anything change. Click Import, and confirm.

13
00:01:41,069 --> 00:01:45,698
The import is complete. Open the student list to check the new students.

14
00:01:46,893 --> 00:01:53,902
Remember the order: upload, check, fix, and only then import. Next, we invite the teachers.
